# Phase 6: Project Testing

## Project Name
FitBuddy

## Objective of Testing
Testing is performed to make sure that the FitBuddy application works correctly and produces the expected results.

## Test Cases

| Test Case | Input | Expected Result | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Open application | Application should open | Pass |
| 2 | Open API documentation | FastAPI Swagger page should appear | Pass |
| 3 | Enter valid fitness details | Fitness plan should be generated | To Test |
| 4 | Enter incomplete details | System should handle the input properly | To Test |
| 5 | Submit fitness form | Backend should receive the request | To Test |
| 6 | Generate plan | Result should be displayed | To Test |

## Testing Methods

### Functional Testing
Checks whether each feature works according to requirements.

### Interface Testing
Checks whether the user interface works correctly.

### Input Testing
Checks different types of user input.

### Error Testing
Checks how the application handles invalid or missing input.

## Result
The basic FastAPI application has been tested successfully. Further testing will be performed after completing the frontend and fitness plan generation features.
